        "id": 5646,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-19T01:26:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So we had an odd occurrence in tonight’s game, Spite had PL531 and Demon’s Kiss in play (in that order) and Absolute Zero had <font color=\"blue\">Subzero Atmosphere</font> in play. Demon’s Kiss did it’s damage at the start of the turn because of <font color=\"blue\">SZA</font> and then PL531 returned ongoing/equipment cards to their owner’s hand, <font color=\"blue\">SZA</font> had to be one of the two… does this mean that all the end of turn effects happen (again) at the end of the turn that now that the effects of <font color=\"blue\">SZA</font> are no longer ongoing or do the villain cards follow the same concept as hero powers and only using each instance of a power once per turn?</p>\n<p>Also as a 4 hero game the first villain card drawn was the PL531 drug (makes you take back equip/ongoing) looked to be a pretty horrible start. A few turns in Tachyon was able to play HUD goggles and Pushing the Limit, pretty much eliminating the effects of that card (and benefiting Tachyon immensely)!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:21.510Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
